1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,550
The Origins of Tea Culture.

2
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:10,687
Tea's discovery is attributed to Chinese Emperor Shen Nung around 2737 BCE, when leaves blew into boiling water.

3
00:00:10,687 --> 00:00:17,025
Chinese tea culture flourished during the Tang Dynasty, establishing elaborate preparation rituals.

4
00:00:17,025 --> 00:00:26,912
Zen Buddhist monks carried tea to Japan, where the chanoyu ceremony elevated steeping into a meditative practice centered on harmony, respect, and tranquility.

5
00:00:26,912 --> 00:00:31,387
Portuguese traders introduced tea to Europe in the 16th century.

6
00:00:31,387 --> 00:00:42,437
In 1840s Britain, afternoon tea formalized as a social institution; British demand reshaped global agriculture, driving plantations across India and Sri Lanka.

7
00:00:42,437 --> 00:00:52,250
Distinct tea cultures now thrive worldwide: mint tea in Morocco, spiced chai in India, bubble tea in Taiwan, and sweet iced tea in the American South.

